cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DrosoMem in research, teaching, software, or derivative analyses, please cite this software and the underlying data sources."
title: "DrosoMem: Sequence Memory in a Fly Connectome"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "CauchyRiemannEquations"
    website: "https://github.com/CauchyRiemannEquations"
abstract: >-
  DrosoMem is exploratory research software for studying sequential recall in
  computational models constrained by Drosophila connectome structure. The
  project evaluates representation, decoding, autonomous recall, structural
  controls, and robustness under explicitly scoped computational experiments.
  It does not claim that living flies memorize mathematical constants, that
  unseen digits are predicted, or that the implemented dynamics constitute a
  validated biological model of memory.
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/CauchyRiemannEquations/DrosoMem"
url: "https://github.com/CauchyRiemannEquations/DrosoMem"
keywords:
  - Drosophila
  - connectome
  - sequence memory
  - reservoir computing
  - neural networks
  - computational neuroscience
  - reproducible research
